{"title":"2012 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part C","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2012 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rowan is given a square grid whose side length is an odd integer. The square is then divided into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> squares,. Rowan shades each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> square along the two diagonals and does not shade any of the remaining squares. For example, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> grid is shown in which Rowan has shaded the squares along the diagonals.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_C&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rowan is given another square grid with odd side length, and the number of 1 by 1 squares that he shades is 41. How many <i>unshaded</i> 1 by 1 squares are there in the grid?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the number of shaded squares for a square grid is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f5a5ded7724c11e58ef212dc3e8549071890a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a whole number representing the number of rows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a5c5d3772d6b4c76f955e254c12563ca27b9ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> because there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> squares for each diagonal, except the center square is repeated twice. Since he shades <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba6cdde56f366d628a7a35826f98523dbe58bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> squares, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c83f4cf85248126cdde986275678d594c827dab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n - 1 = 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aad14c76e16d191abfe9c787eaea6f7d790ce700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n = 41 + 1 = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7ebf5927219002031471b4c45bed579767ec977c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{42}{2} = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>There would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b3925dca6389ad0c78cda0ef6e6948eb98d651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21^{2} = 441$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> squares in total since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> rows and columns. \n</p><p>Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/76326050ece673137fd071f2cc5ddf70065d88f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$441 - 41 = \\boxed{400}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"25\" /> unshaded squares in the grid.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018055301\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 67/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1299/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3012/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.218      1 2012_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%   13.218      1 -total\n 41.34%    5.464      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37085:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018055301 and revision id 286390. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}